>> title: Pulled Roast Chicken
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: chicken, roast, make-ahead, bowl, meal prep
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: pulled chicken, hand-pulled chicken, shredded roast chicken, rotisserie-style chicken, plain roast chicken, chicken for bowls
>> pairs-with: mujaddara, tahini-sauce, basic-vinaigrette
>> servings: 6
>> time: 13 hr
>> step.1: salt uncovered in the fridge 12 hr
>> step.2: roast 425°F (220°C) 35 min, skin up
>> step.3: rest 15 min in the pan
>> step.4: pull it back into its own juices

Salt @boneless chicken thighs{2%lb}(900 g; skin on) with @kosher salt{2%tsp} and leave them on a rack, uncovered, in the fridge ~chill{12%hr}. This is the entire seasoning and it is why the recipe needs no marinade: overnight, the salt draws water out, dissolves in it, and gets pulled back in seasoned all the way through, while the fridge's dry air takes the skin from wet to tacky, which is the difference between skin that browns and skin that steams.

Rub @&(~1)salted thighs{} with @olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} and ~roast{35%min} skin up on a #sheet pan{} at 425°F (220°C), until the skin is the colour of a walnut and the thickest thigh reads 175°F (80°C). Thighs, not breast, and cooked past the temperature a breast would tolerate: the connective tissue in a thigh needs to be up there to melt, and that is what lets you pull it.

Leave @&(~1)roasted thighs{} to ~rest{15%min} in the pan. Do not move them to a board. The juice that comes out belongs in this recipe and a board sends it down the sink.

Pull @&(~1)rested chicken{} apart with two forks **in the pan**, working the shreds through @lemon juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @extra-virgin olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and the fat and juice already there. Chop the skin small and put it back in. Pulled warm, the meat drinks that up and keeps four days; pulled cold, it takes nothing and goes to dry threads in the fridge.
